// PoBSkill is one row of the same hand-written table SkillBaseFlags is dumped from
// (src/Data/Skills/*.lua), carrying the columns ModParser.lua:1605-1612 reads when it builds
// gemIdLookup -- the map that resolves a skill NAMED IN ITEM TEXT to a granted-effect id.
//
// Why the name has to come from here rather than from go-pob-data: PoB keys the lookup on its
// OWN `grantedEffect.name` (:1610), which is not the game's ActiveSkills.DisplayedName. They
// differ on exactly the population :1609's `fromItem` arm exists for -- PoB calls
// SummonVoidSphere "Summon Volatile Anomaly" where go-pob-data calls it "Volatile Anomaly", so
// the item line naming it resolved to nothing at all.
//
// And why the SET has to come from here: poe.GrantedEffects holds 10020 rows against PoB's
// 1526, and the surplus leaks ordinary English words (ignite, backstab, riptide, wildfire,
// taunt, kill, mortar) into a table matched against item text. That is the same class the
// skillNameList fix removed from a different lookup.
//
// The table KEY is the granted-effect id. oracle/skill_flags.lua re-loads src/Data/Skills/*.lua
// into a FRESH table rather than reading the live data.skills, which src/Modules/Data.lua:967-991
// has already mutated; in a fresh load `grantedEffect.id` is still nil, so the key is the only
// place the id survives.
//
// Color is PoB's `grantedEffect.color`: 1=R (strength), 2=G (dexterity), 3=B (intelligence),
// 4=W, and 0 for a skill that declares none. SkillsTab.lua:1236 indexes `{ "R", "G", "B" }` with
// it to decide `matchesSocket`, which is worth data.misc.MatchingSocketQualityBonus (10) of gem
// quality at CalcActiveSkill.lua:545-547 and feeds actualQuality at CalcSetup.lua:1578/:1654.
// ⚠️ IT CANNOT BE DERIVED FROM THE GEM'S TAGS. Colour 4 belongs to item-granted skills
// (src/Data/Skills/glove.lua) and no strength/dexterity/intelligence tag reproduces it.
//
// Legacy, HideFromGemList and PlusVersionOf are what the gem picker filters on
// (GemSelectControl.lua:114-151) and what the gem tooltip's "Legacy Gem" warning reads
// (GemTooltip.lua:242-246).
//
// 1526 skills, 657 hidden, 301 support, 183 fromItem, 27
// fromTree, 1524 with a colour, 1077 admitted by :1609, 36 legacy, 2 hidden from the gem list.
type PoBSkill struct {
	Name            string
	Hidden          bool
	FromItem        bool
	FromTree        bool
	Support         bool
	Color           int
	Legacy          bool
	HideFromGemList bool
	PlusVersionOf   string
}

